WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.033
- [Interviewer] All right, all yours.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.053
- My name is Pete, but I'm
called in Skid Row, Repeat,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.873
because when we have an
encounter you wanna do it again.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.640
If you're on the right side.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.490
And what I mean by the right side is,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.330
if you're not bullying somebody,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.260
or putting somebody down

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.050
because they're less
fortunate than you are

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.940
then I consider that the right side

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.940
because I'm a K9 (indistinct),
a K9 (indistinct)

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.860
is a level of the underdog.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:43.570
I like the person who has
the least chance of winning

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.980
because that's how, I went
through life like that,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.970
having the least chance.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.970
But I started winning
somewhere along the line.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.817
Anyway, before I went into the Navy

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.160
I had got my 70 Buick
Skylark when I was 16,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:10.060
got a 67 Chevy, low rider,
hydraulics the whole works,

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.863
things would go wrong with the car.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.980
I couldn't afford to pay
a mechanic to do things

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.163
now at this time, where
sometimes they didn't want to

00:01:17.163 --> 00:01:19.070
because I liked the money in my pocket.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.670
So I would go out and I would steal cars.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.790
I got good at it, I got real good at it.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.689
I got so good at to where most of the time

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:28.993
I would sit there and I would time myself.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.520
Sometimes I knock on your door,

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.010
and wave at you and walk to your car,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.130
get in before you got outside I was gone.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.450
The longest it took me at
that time was like 18 seconds.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.860
And I've considered that slow.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.060
I'd be in the car and I'm gone

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.920
by the time you run out in
your drawers with your gun

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.280
I didn't care what it was.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.770
It was like a adrenaline test to me,

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:52.223
like a move to manhood,
and I got better at it.

00:01:52.223 --> 00:01:54.600
I also got better at the mechanics.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.860
I couldn't afford to pay a mechanic

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.350
so I had to do it myself.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.900
And when I look at cars,

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.770
it's like I am looking at a
puzzle where I take it apart.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.040
And I remember how it goes back together

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.400
as I take it apart.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.497
When I was younger, seven or eight years,

00:02:06.497 --> 00:02:07.960
I used to take the TV apart.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.600
I couldn't always get it back together

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.550
but I knew how that was supposed to go.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.000
My mom got kinda mad at me

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.440
for taking the electronics
apart in the house,

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.000
but sometimes I put it back
together before she found out.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.000
So there's just a particular time to where

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.660
my brother had a lot of
money, and I had called him up

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.230
because I was at the low end of the scale.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.000
And I told him, "Man,
I need some money, man,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.070
or I'ma go out and I'ma do something.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.830
So he said, "Look, just
meet me at mom's house."

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.220
So I met him at my mom's house.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.451
Couple of hours later, he showed up,

00:02:45.451 --> 00:02:46.410
he told me to get in the car.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.080
And I thought he was just
gonna hand me some money.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.410
Got in the car, and he drove.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.380
We drove for like two
hours out to Lancaster,

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.000
hour and a half, whatever it takes.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.937
And when we got to Lancaster,
we're in his house,

00:02:55.937 --> 00:02:58.070
and the first time I ever seen his house.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:03.050
I had never knew that this dude
had moved up to that level.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:07.300
It was so beautiful, I mean I was amazed.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.500
Large four bedroom, pool
in the back, marble.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.460
I mean, I was looking at this stuff

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.810
and I knew what it costs
because I had went into

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.720
Fred Federated Store, a stereo store,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.370
and they had the Macintosh system.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.960
And the cheapest part of a Macintosh

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.660
was the $204,999, but
he had his whole system.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.137
Anyway, he told me,

00:03:28.137 --> 00:03:31.200
"Just relax, we're gonna
go get some money, right."

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.890
So a day went by, another day went by.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.850
He got me brand new clothes and feed me.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:37.857
And I'm getting kind of tired.

00:03:37.857 --> 00:03:38.860
"When are you gonna give me the money

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.330
so I can go do my own thing?"

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.163
So he said,

00:03:41.163 --> 00:03:43.600
"Okay look, we'll make
the move tomorrow, right."

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.870
So anyway, that evening he came

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.790
with a brand new Honda Accord

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.030
with a dealer's license plate on it,

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.280
he went and purchased it.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.090
He took me downtown LA,
where I'm about now,

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.380
and we went to the
Japanese or the Chinese, or

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.490
we went to the Asian section
and he bought a Ninja suit.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.003
He bought, you know, the whole hookup.

00:04:05.003 --> 00:04:06.380
I'm tripping off of it,

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.490
and wondering what he gonna do.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:13.100
So that night he gave,
he said his 38 is jammed,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.020
so I took it apart,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.220
I mean, at this time I
was good with weapons.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:19.160
I took it apart, oiled it, cleaned it.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.690
We went out in the desert and fired it.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.160
Cleaned it again, put it back together.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.020
That morning, we got in
the car and we took off.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:30.260
We drove for like 18 hours, 19 hours,

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.610
20 hours, to somewhere around Oklahoma.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:38.483
And we pulled up in a
certain area and he said,

00:04:39.447 --> 00:04:41.250
"That's him right there."

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.390
So I looked around and
see who we talking about.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.930
He said, "There, the green Cadillac."

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.610
So in the green Cadillac I seen a dude,

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.720
and he gets out, he go to
a bar and grill pool hall.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:50.553
He opens it up, he goes in.

00:04:50.553 --> 00:04:51.980
He said, "Yeah, he own that building.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.460
That's his whole hookup right there."

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.160
He said, "Look, I gave
this dude a small fortune

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.340
and he owed me and he never paid me.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.710
He keep telling me he gonna pay me

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.680
but he not giving it to me, fuck that."

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.650
He said, "We're gonna take him down."

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.160
I'm like, "All right, I'm good with that."

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.400
So he said, "Let me show
you something else."

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.390
We went to another part of town

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:12.470
and this is physically the
first time I ever seen police

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.380
in somebody's pocket.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.440
What I mean by that is the
dudes were serving dope

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.820
and police sitting there,
and they not doing nothing.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.040
I was amazed that they didn't
jump out and bust them.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.560
Matter of fact, the
dude opened up his sack

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.490
on the police car, took some work out,

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.050
gave it to somebody, got the money,

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.290
and went back talking to the police.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:29.270
I was like, "Wow, that's amazing."

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.580
He said, yeah, he got the whole force

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.270
like that in his pocket, right?

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.130
So he said, "Let me show
you where his sister live."

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.690
We went to his sister's place,

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:41.660
and he said, "He keeps at least two birds

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.990
in her kitchen under the sink."

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.970
A bird is a kilo, a
brick, a thousand grams.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:47.630
He said, "He keep at least two of them."

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.410
A thousand grands at
this time was $25,000.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.450
You'd make a $100,000 off of it.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:56.640
You'd literally make
a $100,000 off a kilo.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.700
So anyway, he say, "She keep two of them.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.380
He keep two of them in her kitchen

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.930
and taped under the sink."

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:05.250
He said, "He also keep
one or two in his house

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.790
under the sink, but it's
outside in the garage, right."

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:11.190
So we went and we drove to
another section and we pulled up.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.920
He said, "Okay, that's
his house right there."

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.240
He said, "This is what you're gonna do."

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.370
We pulled off.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:17.557
He said, "I think he live by himself,

00:06:17.557 --> 00:06:18.890
but you gotta check it out."

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.430
So we pulled off two or three miles.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:25.640
He pulled over, he gave me the Ninja suit,

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.370
he gave me the 380, he gave me $500.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.200
He said, "I'll see you when you get home."

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.730
He got out of the car and
he started walking away.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:36.020
I just looked at him while he walked off.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:38.200
After he got to the corner,
I knew he wasn't joking.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.160
He turned the corner and disappeared.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.120
So I'm looking around thinking,

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:42.150
"This motherfucker
think I'm gonna do this.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.650
Okay, that's how he want it,
he want me to do it on my own.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.580
All right, fantastic, I'll put it down."

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.230
So got in the driver's seat, drove around.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:51.570
Now I remember the section
where the pool hall was.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.390
So I went back over to that section,

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.550
and I watched the dude serve him.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.140
They would go after they
served him till they sat,

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.740
they'd go over there to his bar and grill.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:01.630
They come back out and
they start serving again.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:04.570
So I knew those is...
work he had four guys.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.870
So that night, when they
left the bar and grill,

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.330
they serve out of their home.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.220
So I went to their house
and I didn't know him.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:13.270
So I kind of waited down the
street till somebody came by.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.103
I said, "Hey, you feeling to go down there

00:07:14.103 --> 00:07:14.936
and get something?"

00:07:14.936 --> 00:07:15.769
They say, "Yeah."

00:07:15.769 --> 00:07:16.602
I said, "What's dude's name?"

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:17.810
And they would tell me his name.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:18.643
I said, "Look, I wanna go with you,

00:07:18.643 --> 00:07:19.577
I wanna get something for like a $100.

00:07:19.577 --> 00:07:21.030
"All right, come on."

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.520
So I would walk with him.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.170
I would go in, I would make a purchase

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.090
and let the dude see me a couple of times.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.410
Then I went on my own.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.350
I let the dude know that I was
gonna buy something larger.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.210
I let them know that,
"Hey, my name is Chicago.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.670
We trying to do something big.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:35.503
If you can handle the weight

00:07:35.503 --> 00:07:37.680
I'm gonna go ahead and start
purchasing bird for you."

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.280
These dudes wanting to excel,
they wanted to grow up.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.570
All of them did.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:46.270
So I went back to them, I
started shortstopping the people,

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.250
the people would have to walk like

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.120
two or three miles to get to a spot.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.900
So I went down the road and parked,

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:51.890
and started serving them down the road

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.520
and I'd go down there
and buy some from them.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.710
So I built up my clientele
through them for about nine days.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.840
Every night I knew what
time this dude closed up.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.390
So I would go sit outside the bar.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:02.910
When he drive home, I'd follow him.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.460
He'd go in the store, he'd
get a pack of Benson &amp; Hedges,

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.840
get two forty-ounce of Old
English, and he'd go home.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.290
And I'll follow him home.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.400
The second time I followed him home

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.480
I jumped the gate and I took the trash.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.450
I took his trash because
the trash would tell you

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.320
who an individual is, how
many people are there,

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.230
who lives there and so forth and so on.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.720
So I took the trash and I went through it.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.500
I know he lived by himself now.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.260
I know there's no woman, no children

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.200
'cause he has no trash
for women and children.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.110
There's no lipstick on his
cigarettes and anything else.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.180
So I know pretty much
when he leaves for work

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.560
the house is empty.

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:35.777
So after about nine
days, I make a decision.

00:08:35.777 --> 00:08:37.280
"I'm going to go and get this dude.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.080
This is the night I'm gonna get him."

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.100
'Cause he's a creature of habit,

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:42.800
he was doing the same thing
the same way every time.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:45.410
So the ninth day I went to go and get him

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.810
but I decided I'm gonna go in the house

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.180
I'ma find the money.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:51.510
So he had a stucco stout house.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.720
So I took a screwdriver

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.500
and dug the stucco away from no bars,

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:57.980
pulled the bars out, climbed
in and searched the house.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.270
I searched the house for
about a hour, hour and a half.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.810
And I found a sack of
money, but it was $1 bills.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.710
It was just like 4,000 $1
bills off in the closet.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:07.977
So I took it, I threw it back in.

00:09:07.977 --> 00:09:09.100
That wasn't what I was there for.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.650
I knew he keep anywhere from a quarter

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.310
to a whole meal ticket inside his house

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:16.370
from $250,000 to a million
dollars inside his house

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.160
'cause he never made deposits in the bank.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.240
So I decided I'm gonna have
to take this the hard way.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.700
I couldn't find the money.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:25.290
So I had to wait for him to come home.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.617
So I called my brother and I told him,

00:09:26.617 --> 00:09:29.550
"Hey look, I'm finna make this jump

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:30.610
and take him down if I got to."

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.770
He said, "Look man, this dude is a killer.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:36.060
If you slip, he gonna get you.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.160
So if somebody's gotta go

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.550
it might as well be him instead of you."

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.820
I said, "all right, I got it covered."

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.300
I waited for the guy to come home.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.250
He eventually came home,
and when he came through,

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.530
I had a ski mask on, I rushed him.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:48.900
I rushed him like I was the police.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.000
I handcuffed him, hit him in the head,

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:51.833
turned him over and told him,

00:09:51.833 --> 00:09:54.363
"Hey look, you got one
chance to live through this,

00:09:54.363 --> 00:09:55.730
tell me where the money is

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:58.100
or I'm gonna blow your
motherfucking brains out."

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.470
He told me it was in the
mattress in the bedroom.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:03.300
I had felt the mattress,
but I didn't feel the money.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:06.806
So I went back, cut the
mattress, and there it was,

00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:11.566
it was $186,000, 186 stacks
of thousand dollars bills.

00:10:11.566 --> 00:10:13.810
Each stack with a $1,000.

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.756
I put them all in a bag, left the house.

00:10:16.756 --> 00:10:18.340
But before I left the house,

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:22.660
I went back in and I got the
two kilos from under the sink.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.730
So I got a $186,00 and 2 kilos.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.930
When I leave the house,
jump in the Honda Accord

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.440
I hit the highway.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.300
I'm doing about 110 'cause I'm happy

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.790
I got dizzy and a 110 miles
an hour on the freeway

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:34.760
with two birds sitting out,

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:38.440
and $186,000 on the driver's seat.

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:41.920
When I get back home I
don't run into my brother

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.590
for about a day, I'm trying
to catch up with him.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.160
I don't run into him.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.870
So at this time I go and I do another move

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.010
with $186,000 cash and two birds.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.160
I go and do something else, I add to it.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.580
I get another half a bird and $64,000.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:57.360
So when I started doing it,
was I found it was easier

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.190
to start robbing the
people who sell the dope

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.620
than it was to rob.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.910
I mean, it's not like
they was gonna go tell

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.780
or call the police and
say they got robbed.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.390
Anyway, there was this one thing

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:11.330
that kinda went down bad.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.950
Not that I had to hurt
somebody or somebody hurt me,

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:17.383
but it went South of the border.

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:22.350
It turned out that there
was a female in the house

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:26.180
when I thought it was a dude,
and she kind of surprised me.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.270
She surprised me by walking in

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.720
when I thought the house
was supposed to be empty.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.250
And I didn't put a whole in her per say,

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:39.510
but I almost did, close enough to it,

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:43.330
to where she backed up and fell out

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:44.580
the second storey window.

00:11:45.711 --> 00:11:49.040
And when I looked out she was tangled up

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:52.610
in the bushes downstairs,
and she didn't die,

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.870
but she was injured real bad.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:56.763
And I made a decision from that time that

00:11:56.763 --> 00:12:00.439
that was the end of
that, I wouldn't be doing

00:12:00.439 --> 00:12:03.700
what they call now home invasions.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.450
I wasn't doing a home
invasion on people who

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.600
just the regular, you know, citizen.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.350
I was doing a home invasion on the ones

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:14.240
who had the money, and I
knew they had the money.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:15.860
And I would go in, and most of them were,

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.290
all of them, actually all
of them were dope dealers.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:20.543
So I would go in and
I would liberate them.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:27.970
Eventually I did plug somebody

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.680
but I'm not gonna really go into that

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.350
because there's no statute limitation

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.540
on a variety of things.

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.860
And that's not one of the
ones I'm going to go into

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:40.680
but I wish I wouldn't have.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.670
I wish I didn't.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:45.120
I never got pinned for it,
and probably never will,

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:49.450
because three people can keep a secret

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:50.650
if two of them are dead.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.160
And that would be the only way,

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.550
so I did everything by myself.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.670
I didn't take nobody with me,

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.840
if I did I probably
would've got rid of them too

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.183
unless it was an immediate family member.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.720
But I'm not particularly proud

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:07.830
of a lot of things that I did.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.270
And this was 15, 16 years old

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:13.600
when I really didn't have to do it, at 17,

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.730
I didn't have to do it,
but I did it any way.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.490
I did it because it was
more of an exhilaration.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.390
There was something to break the norm,

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.880
something to test my limited abilities

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:28.750
when I didn't think I was mortal,

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:30.700
I thought I was immortal.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.930
But I found out when I
did go into the military

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.980
and got scrambled and got hurt,

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:41.253
it did hurt that I was mortal.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:45.960
That pain was nothing compared
to what happened to me

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.293
about three weeks ago.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.390
I was sitting in front of
a car in a lounge chair

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.600
and I had my feet out about 12 inches.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.590
And a Hummer H2 came down the street

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.430
and actually ran over my foot.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.500
And I'm only 12 inches out from the car.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.050
My foot is 12 inches out.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.720
He ran over my right foot,

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.560
and I heard a boom first.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.610
And I thought he had ran over my shin

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:13.690
but it was only my foot.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.270
And when he ran over my
foot, I couldn't believe it.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.620
I didn't feel the pain immediately,

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.780
until I stood up and
realized what had happened.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.930
And I looked down and
I could see the print

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.420
the Hummer tyres, the (indistinct) tryes,

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.400
I can see it in my shoe.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.700
And I knew that same print was in my foot.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:31.130
I knew my foot was shaped
like that, like a cartoon.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:34.647
And I jumped up and my
girlfriend had said,

00:14:34.647 --> 00:14:36.090
"Did that car hit the chair?

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:36.923
I heard a boom."

00:14:36.923 --> 00:14:39.114
I said, "That boom was my fuckin' foot."

00:14:39.114 --> 00:14:44.114
(laughs) I've never felt pain like that.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:48.170
I fell down and I took my shoe off

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.960
and I looked at my foot and
it was like an accordion man.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.390
And I pulled the other shoe
off just for a comparison,

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.490
and I looked at them, and the right one

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.520
is different from the left one.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:01.270
He ran over my foot
literally broke my right foot

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:03.690
and two of my toes, and he kept going.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.400
Police, ambulance, everybody came.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.860
I cussed everybody out (laughs).

00:15:08.787 --> 00:15:10.890
I fear God, but I was cussing Him out too

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.640
for letting it happen.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.060
He ran over my foot, he broke it,

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.360
and I've never felt.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.210
I mean, I used to walk
in the street blindly.

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:19.760
I used to just ride with reckless abandon.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:22.730
Now when I walk in the street,
I stay on the sidewalk.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.430
And when I cross, I look behind me

00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:27.490
because that shit hurted.

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:29.010
And it still hurts now.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.070
And it's been about three weeks.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:34.670
I couldn't let 'em put a cast on me

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.360
because if they'd put a cast on me,

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:38.610
I would've literally starved to death.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.840
Who would went and got my meals?

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:40.980
Who would have hustled for me?

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:42.820
I would have been in trouble.

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:45.322
So I kind of braved through the pain

00:15:45.322 --> 00:15:49.030
and everything else and
limped where I needed to go

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:50.710
and limped to do what I had to do.

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:53.210
And I did a few things.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:57.280
But when you live by the sword,

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:58.320
you die by the sword, you know.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:03.320
It comes hard, and easy come, easy go.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:07.710
And I appreciate the opportunity to

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.550
be able to divulge some things.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.790
Some things are interesting.

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.940
other things are casual,

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.590
but here all you have to do

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.990
is sit back and look down the street

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:22.280
and you will see a movie unfold.

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:24.290
Something's gonna happen.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:28.027
Skid Row, downtown Los
Angeles, this is where we at.

00:16:28.027 --> 00:16:29.930
And I can appreciate being here

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:33.050
because once you,

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.330
what's the sign say?

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:37.470
I lived through the earthquake,

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.420
I've conquered this.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:42.610
Once you lived through Skid
Row, you've lived, man.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.630
You can live just about anywhere now

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.360
if you know the language.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.450
But there's a Skid Row,
South Central Los Angeles.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:50.930
And I appreciate your time.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.470
I appreciate your attention.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:55.660
